null,"unit_id":"agent:T5c","usage":{"input_tokens":30321,"output_tokens":1291,"requests":3}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"9f41a73148fc09b45e58818a57cf9f46cd8c66da5d7d856dd9c00949d429d095"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:project.symbol-reference-completeness","usage":{"input_tokens":37903,"output_tokens":1352,"requests":3}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"698a34404606a7e78c4f278f8b9fcc3adf129b5b727a265376ad8eea2caa2b96"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:G6","usage":{"input_tokens":136465,"output_tokens":5232,"requests":7}}],"version":1},"findings":[{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["6 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable).","vague/subjective terms present: sufficient"],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Reconcile the Approach's comparison-dimension claims with what the single-mutation, provenance-verbatim serialize_manifest oracle can actually verify: either scope the claim to payload-field parity + construction rejection, or extend the mechanism (multi-mutation manifests for ordering; a typed projection over provenance-borne follow-on/suppression/retry/final-state) so each enumerated dimension is genuinely tested rather than guaranteed-identical by construction.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.4333,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["payload_shadow.compare_scenario serializes each twin as a single-element list ([legacy_mut] / [typed_mut]), so serialize_manifest's sort key (direction.value, action.value, target) — identical between twins — never orders anything across a batch","Both twins receive provenance=dict(scenario['provenance']) verbatim; corpus README states provenance is 'untyped by ADR 0107 — carries follow_on/suppression/retry/reason metadata unchanged by this story', so provenance-borne dimensions are byte-identical by construction, not by parity verification","Context claims the deliverable is 'sufficient deterministic parity evidence to make the later cutover/deletion safe'"],"finding":"The Approach enumerates comparison dimensions the chosen mechanism cannot actually exercise: ordering (single-mutation manifests never trigger serialize_manifest's batch sort), and follow-ons/suppression/retry-dispositions/modeled-final-state (carried in the untyped provenance dict that is copied verbatim into both twins, so byte-identity is guaranteed by construction, not verified). The oracle only meaningfully verifies payload-field parity and construction-time rejection.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"faee9843711fe4c09","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach, bullets 3-4 ('Drive legacy and typed planning/serialization over identical observations' / 'Compare ordering, fields, identity scopes, diagnostics, follow-ons, suppression, retry dispositions, and modeled final state')","norm_id":"n6f508bfbc2a9e955","priority":0.3667,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A future producer emits a batch of mutations whose typed-vs-legacy ORDERING diverges under sort — the shadow corpus would not catch it because it only compares single-mutation manifests","A cutover that also moves follow-on/suppression/retry data out of provenance into typed fields would find the shadow corpus proved nothing about those dimensions"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.6667,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"incomplete_enumeration","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Restate the Approach to reflect that this story compares a typed-payload wrapper's round-trip against its legacy-dict twin over a hand-authored corpus (not two live planners over shared observations), and note explicitly that producer-emitted-shape fidelity rests on the corpus being hand-verified against producer code rather than captured from it.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.4944,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["mutation_payloads.build_typed_payload derives the typed payload from the SAME legacy dict the legacy twin uses (payload_cls.from_legacy(payload)), and serialize_manifest projects it back via as_legacy_dict() — a round-trip of one input, not two planners over one observation","AC7 and mutation_payloads.py module docstring state no producer/planner is rewired in this story ('production continues constructing legacy dict payloads')","corpus README: scenarios are 'informed by (but not a literal recording of)' producers — no producer is actually executed"],"finding":"The Approach describes 'Drive legacy and typed planning/serialization over identical observations,' implying two independent planning paths compared for parity; but the plan (and AC7) keeps production emitting only legacy dicts and never wires a typed planner. The typed side is a wrapper re-derived from the legacy dict (from_legacy -> as_legacy_dict), so the oracle is a round-trip fidelity check on the wrapper, not a comparison of two planning implementations. The Approach wording overstates what the mechanism establishes.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fa84963e148686b31","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach, bullet 3 ('Drive legacy and typed planning/serialization over identical observations. Capture canonical normalized intent/outcome traces without invoking either writer.')","norm_id":"n06efc1cb55028a0f","priority":0.3056,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A reviewer relying on the Approach prose expects planner-level parity evidence; the mechanism instead proves wrapper round-trip fidelity, which does not exercise the producers' own field-selection/exclusion logic"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5556,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementat